WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Mendel followed two pea traits
at once: round or wrinkled seeds,

2
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.280
yellow or green.

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:11.390
He counted 315 round
yellow, 108 round green,

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.740
101 wrinkled yellow and 32 wrinkled green.

5
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.170
His two genes were on
different chromosomes,

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.500
so they assorted independently.

7
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.150
But genes on the same
chromosome are linked:

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.340
their alleles travel together.

9
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.350
So if two genes sit on
the same chromosome,

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.500
can they ever be separated?

11
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.690
In this mission, you'll see how
chromosome pairs line up in meiosis,

12
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.130
so unlinked genes mix freely.

13
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.890
Then you'll follow two linked
genes on one pair of chromosomes,

14
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.690
as meiosis begins.

15
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:48.350
Your mission: find out whether two genes on
the same chromosome can ever be separated.
